{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 35, :comments ["<b>And his hand falters (ומטה ידו).</b> From the same root as לא ימוט; the mem is a root letter, and like it is אם אמרתי מטה רגלי." "<b>Your brother (אחיך).</b> An Israelite." "<b>With you (עמך).</b> For you are obligated to be present with him when you see him." "<b>And you shall hold him up (והחזקת בו).</b> The opposite of his hand falters, so that he does not fall." "<b>Ger and toshav (גר ותושב).</b> And if he is from your land, or a ger and toshav." "<b>And he shall live (וחי).</b> Like יחיה."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:12:27.126142993Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}